  <section class="content-section">
    <p class="page-kicker">When Sennheiser Momentum 4 wins</p>
    <h2 class="section-heading">Pick Sennheiser Momentum 4 if...</h2>
    <p>Audio quality matters to you as much as ANC. The Momentum 4 has a warmer, more detailed sound with better bass control and more clarity in vocals. If you actually listen to music between calls, the difference is obvious.</p><p>You use them all day and hate charging. 60 hours vs 40 hours is a real difference — Sennheiser lasts through a week of workdays; Anker needs a mid-week top-up.</p><p>You have a Snapdragon phone or Android device supporting aptX Adaptive. The Sennheiser sounds noticeably better over aptX than the Anker does over AAC.</p><p>Build feels premium. Materials, hinges, cushion quality — the Sennheiser is built to last five years of daily use. The Anker is built to last two.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="content-section">
    <p class="page-kicker">When Anker Soundcore Q30 wins</p>
    <h2 class="section-heading">Pick Anker Soundcore Q30 if...</h2>
    <p>You want ANC for a specific limited purpose (commute, occasional flight, focus block) and don't need the best audio quality. The Anker's ANC is a real 22-25 dB reduction — 80% of what the Sennheiser does at 20% of the price.</p><p>You lose or damage headphones. Kids, active lifestyle, prone-to-leaving-them-at-airports — $70 replacements sting way less than $350 replacements.</p><p>You want to try ANC before spending. The Anker is the cheapest credible way to find out if ANC actually helps your specific noise environment. If it does, upgrade to Sennheiser later.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="content-section">
    <p class="page-kicker">The verdict</p>
    <p>Buy the Sennheiser if premium ANC audio is your primary music setup and you'll use them for years. Buy the Anker if you want credible ANC on a budget and don't need audiophile-tier sound.</p><p>Do not buy either if your priority is call microphone quality — AirPods Max is the correct answer there. Both of these have adequate but not great call mics.</p>
  </section>

